  "question": {
    "text": "A thin rod of negligible mass and area of cross-section <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, suspended vertically from one end, has a length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>0.5</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The rod is cooled to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;but prevented from contracting by attaching a mass at the lower end. The value of this mass is<br />\r(Given, coefficient of linear expansion is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, Young's modulus is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and<sup>&nbsp;</sup><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "40",
  "solution": {
    "text": "The change in length due to decrease in temperature,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#916;</mo><msub><mtext>l</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>L</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>&#916;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#916;</mo><msub><mtext>l</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></math> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ... (i)<br /><br />Negative sign implies that length is decreasing. Now let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> be the mass attached to the lower end. Then, change in length due to suspension of load is<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#916;</mo><msub><mtext>l</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mtext>Mg</mtext></mfenced><mtext>L</mtext></mrow><mtext>AY</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mtext>M</mtext></mfenced><mfenced><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mtext>0.5</mtext></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#916;</mo><msub><mtext>l</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mtext>1.25</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;... (ii)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#916;</mo><msub><mtext>l</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>&#916;</mo><msub><mtext>l</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mtext>1.25</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mtext>0.5</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; (from equations (i) and (ii))<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac linethickness=\"1\"><mrow><mtext>0.5</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mtext>1.25</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>",
    "image": null
